    "text_delta": "fessional risk:** Municipal planning is a relatively small, interconnected field. Accusing a panel of bias based on its gender composition can be perceived as professional bitterness and may damage your reputation across regional municipalities.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n* **Follow up cordially:** Send a polite, professional follow-up email to HR or the search coordinator inquiring about feedback. Frame it around personal professional development:\n  > *\"I understand you are likely busy finalizing the appointment, but I would greatly appreciate any high-level feedback the panel might have on how I can strengthen my profile for future executive opportunities.\"*\n* **Accept high-level feedback:** If they provide feedback, focus on areas like executive leadership, presentation, or public engagement rather than debating technical qualifications.\n* **Move forward:** Reaching the final three and completing two rounds of interviews for a municipal director role indicates your credentials and experience are highly competitive. Focus that momentum on the next opportunity.\n",
